{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB extension cables fit my ongoing use of keyboards, card readers, and external drives because they could make the equipment I already use easier to connect.",
    "The Blink doorbell feels like a useful next step because it adds entrance video to my basic door security and works with the Alexa devices I already have."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another Fire TV stick, same-generation Echo Dot, or Echo Show would mostly repeat functions covered by my recent purchases, so familiarity alone does not give me a reason to buy.",
    "The camera bundles ask me to add several cameras when I only see a clear need at the entrance. Earbuds, a small television, and a themed remote cover do not address a current need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any Alexa-related device, even when it duplicates something I recently bought.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in more electronics, without enough attention to the particular job each purchase serves."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Buying a Show 5 stand after the Show 5 suggests I am completing that setup; it does not mean I am ready to replace it with a larger display.",
    "I am interested in practical additions that solve a specific problem, such as extending USB reach or seeing who is at the door, and would start with one useful device before buying a whole security bundle."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my Alexa and computer-accessory interests but often confused completing my existing setup with wanting more devices that do the same thing."
}"}
